WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
On Helvellyn's east face,
in the Lake District,

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.090
a small lake fills a
deep hollow: Red Tarn,

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.950
25.6 metres deep.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.750
Beside it rise two knife-edge ridges:
Striding Edge and Swirral Edge.

5
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.190
Helvellyn's eastern slopes
hold nine of these hollows.

6
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:24.190
At Nethermost Cove, the back
wall is 280 metres high.

7
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.790
And the rock is hard: Borrowdale
Volcanic lavas and ashes,

8
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.230
about 450 million years old.

9
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.590
So what scooped out these hollows?

10
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.610
Were they once volcano craters?

11
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.170
Did rivers cut them?

12
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.930
In this mission, you'll
map the Lake District,

13
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.110
read its rocks, and name each landform.

14
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.970
Then you'll draw how one
of these hollows forms,

15
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.750
step by step.

16
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.690
Your mission: find out what
carved Helvellyn's hollows.
